\lispPackageChapter{livermore/xcs-analyzer}

The \texttt{livermore/xcs-analyzer} package is a combined environment and
reinforcement program that scores actions and keeps a running history of
correctness.  Most single-step problems subclass \texttt{analyzer} and
define \texttt{correct-action} and \texttt{get-situation}.

\section{Classes}

\lispClassSubsection{analyzer}

Subclass of both \texttt{environment} and \texttt{reinforcement-program}.

\begin{description}
\item[\texttt{current-situation}] The situation most recently presented.
\item[\texttt{number-of-situations}] How many situations have been presented.
\item[\texttt{current-action}] The action most recently taken.
\item[\texttt{actions}] How many actions have been taken.
\item[\texttt{correct-actions}] How many of those were correct.
\item[\texttt{action-history}] \texttt{t} or \texttt{nil} for each action,
  newest first.
\item[\texttt{odd-action-history}] The same history for odd-numbered actions.
\item[\texttt{even-action-history}] The same history for even-numbered actions.
\end{description}

\section{Methods}

\lispGenericSubsection{correct-action}

The action that should have been taken.  The default method signals an
error; define this for each problem.

\lispGenericSubsection{correct-action?}

True if \texttt{current-action} equals \texttt{correct-action}.

\lispGenericSubsection{get-reward}

Returns $1000.0$ for a correct action and $0.0$ otherwise.

\lispGenericSubsection{execute-action}

Records the action, updates the correctness counts, and prints a short
running report, including the last fifty actions split into odd and even
trials.
